# Executed experiments and evidence scope

This English ledger separates scientific questions and version identities. The source closeout status is `CLOSED_EXPLORATORY_WITH_LIMITATIONS`; original acceptance is separate from publication verification. The [history](../../archive/HISTORY.md) retains the earlier hidden-direction study and substantive negative findings. The machine-readable [ledger](results/experiment_ledger.csv) remains a versioned evidence index.

| Stage | Question and data level | Representation, readout and split | Result and scope | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Original reproduction/tool choice | Published condition-mean coordinate decoding and cross-half response preservation | Original FA50/OLS reference; separate AE/GPFA 47/16/16 Ridge comparison | The pilot reproduced the published outputs. GPFA64 was a historical tool choice under a parameter cap, without matched protocols or a universal-optimality claim. | [Historical account](../../archive/HISTORY.md#original-reproduction-and-representation-selection) |
| Early average-behavior proxy | Continuous path construction and short-window deviation decoding | Frozen GPFA64, screened conditions, Ridge, 47/16/16 | The single preview established construction continuity. Small test sets and delta amplitude failures limited neural interpretation. | [Proxy history](../../archive/HISTORY.md#early-average-behavior-proxy) |
| Old all-79 segmented candidate | Each complete path's own-target reconstruction | Frozen GPFA64, OLS, 100 nominal 39/40 splits | Small full-path candidate improvements occurred with few behavior-active bins; older representation fitting overlapped some readout test conditions. | [Segmented history](../../archive/HISTORY.md#old-all-79-segmented-candidate-ols) |
| Trial-endpoint version | Individual behavioral targets on repeated condition-mean neural input | Per-split train-39 FA50/GPFA50, OLS | Route B supplies no paired single-trial neural evidence. Repeated rows increase record-rich conditions' contribution. | [Version comparison](../condition_endpoint_fa_gpfa_v1/results/previous_trial_version_comparison.csv) |
| Current endpoint means | One condition-by-time input and one fixed mean target | Same stored FA50/GPFA50, OLS, same splits | All four full-interval results favor objective paths. Target variance and condition weighting changed together. | [Current report](../condition_endpoint_fa_gpfa_v1/REPORT.md) |
| A: own-target and cross-scoring | Both heads scored against both targets | Saved test-only predictions; no fitting | Replayed full scores and all four cells. A has no randomized null distribution. | [A table](results/A/cross_2x2_summary.csv) |
| B: fixed-readout mismatch | Correct condition correspondence on matched time support | 1000 repeats x 100 splits; no readout or representation refit | Matched scores exceed mismatches; changing overlap limits exact permutation inference and does not isolate behavior. | [Validation](results/B/B_validation.json), [summary](results/B/B_summary.csv) |
| C: random endpoints | New endpoint targets with original condition geometry | 1000 allocations x 100 splits; new OLS fits, fixed representations | Actual candidates exceed the random reference in primary ranges. Post-collision RMSE and geometry-baseline skill retain phase exceptions. | [Completion](results/C/completed.json), [summary](results/C/random_endpoint_summary.csv) |

The mean-endpoint geometry baseline exceeds all four full-interval objective and candidate reconstructions. Perle candidate skill is slightly positive for GPFA50 hidden samples and FA50/GPFA50 no-collision samples. These exceptions are retained in the [final report](FINAL_REPORT.md#mean-endpoint-geometry-baseline).

The original experiment records establish completion of the entries above. Repeated splits/randomizations do not increase independent neural trial counts. `raw_preprocessing=fail`, unknown neural membership, terminal timing uncertainty and estimated collision anchors remain. The future grouped-neural design was not executed.
